# Project rules — Cloudy game starter kit

You are working in a small, original browser game kit from Cloudy.

## Style
- Keep the code readable. Prefer clear names and short functions over cleverness.
- Tunable numbers live at the top of game.js. Change those first when asked for feel tweaks.
- Do not add a bundler, framework, or new library unless the user explicitly asks. Orbit Garden already vendors Three.js; leave that as a static file.
- Art and sound must stay original or generated in code (canvas drawings, Web Audio beeps). Do not add copyrighted, trademarked, or ripped game assets.

## Changes
- Make the smallest diff that lands the request. No drive-by rewrites of the game loop.
- Match the existing style (vanilla JS, no build step). Keep index.html, audio.js, and boot.js working.
- Preserve `window.__CLOUDY_KIT__`, `bootKit`, `tickKit`, and the `?autostart=1` hook so tests still run.
- If you add a mechanic, also add a way to verify it (on-screen state, a comment in the README, or a short playtest note).

## Scope
- Do not change the MIT license or add personal names, emails, or phone numbers.
- Update README.md when you change controls, file layout, or how to run the kit.

## Cellar Crawl notes
- Turns are discrete. Do not quietly turn it into a real-time action game unless asked.
- Keep FOV and the seen-map so exploration still feels like a roguelike.
